{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Seek to negotiate a reciprocal UK-EU 6-month free travel agreement",
        "additional_details": "We call on the UK Government to seek to negotiate a mutually beneficial, reciprocal free travel agreement with the European Union that balances travel rights equally between UK and EU citizens.\r\n\r\nWe feel current restrictions heavily impact thousands of UK citizens who own holiday homes in the EU, individuals visiting friends and family for extended periods, and retirees traveling in motorhomes or boats. The Government should actively push for parity.",
        "background": "Currently, UK citizens are restricted to the 90/180-day rule when visiting the Schengen Area. We feel this creates a severe imbalance, as EU citizens are permitted to visit the UK for a continuous period of up to 6 months without a visa. ",
